      "id": "qpwj25h",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "2. Longitudes"
    },
    {
      "id": "hg0x286",
      "type": "image",
      "imageId": "pqtm0bo",
      "src": "/books/Guide/GS & GK GUIDE BOOK/images/image_pqtm0bo.jpeg"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "oad17n7",
      "content": "<img></img>• Longitudes are imaginary vertical lines joining North and South poles."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "juld9l7",
      "content": "• They measure distance east or west of the Prime Meridian."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "m8k6yaa",
      "content": "• The Prime Meridian is located at Greenwich, London."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "u8xooj6",
      "content": "• There are 360° of longitude."
    },
    {
      "id": "czyqurk",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "3. Indian Standard Time (IST)"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "w4jv920",
      "content": "• India follows Indian Standard Time."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "2mdda12",
      "content": "• The standard meridian is 82°30′ East longitude.       "
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "amuoknz",
      "content": "• It passes near Mirzapur in Uttar Pradesh."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "hbm8dwj",
      "content": "• IST is 5 hours 30 minutes ahead of GMT."
    },
    {
      "type": "pullQuote",
      "content": "Indian Standard Time is calculated on the basis of 82.5° E longitude which passes through Mirzapur in Uttar Pradesh.",
      "id": "ot8pa6q"
    },
